        <div class="feature-card__title">{item.title}</div>
        <p>{item.body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    Put scope, price and revision limits in writing, take a deposit on larger jobs, and price any new request separately. Check the official GST and Udyam portals for the current rules and whether they apply to you, since clients abroad can be treated differently. If you are choosing between this route and a job, read
    <a href="/blog/freelancing-business/freelancing-vs-job-india-which-is-better/">freelancing vs job in India</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-pays">Who pays for these freelance skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    A startup or small firm pays developers and designers to build something, an online brand pays marketers for leads or sales, and a creator or brand that posts every week pays an editor. Owners pay analysts and finance helpers for clear monthly numbers, and a firm with a slow manual task pays someone who can hand it to an AI tool. Upwork only brings you to them and takes a fee.
  </p>

  <p>
    Each payer checks proof first: a live build or a short test task for developers, ad or report results for marketers and analysts, and a sample reel for editors. The first basic skill is a one-page offer with who you help, what you deliver, what it costs and one proof. Then follow up, ask each happy client for a referral and name your price calmly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and these skills</h2>

  <p>
    AI cuts the routine layer of every skill in this list, and it also creates new paid work. Upwork reported that earnings from skills naming AI grew 109% in 2025, with AI video generation and editing up 329% and AI integration up 178%.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Start now</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Use AI for first drafts in your skill, then test and correct every output yourself.</li>
        <li>Keep a note of what the AI got wrong and how you caught it.</li>
        <li>Pick one real client problem and solve it end to end with AI helping.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Build toward</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Owning a result for a client, such as leads or a working system.</li>
        <li>Building workflows others pay to run, with checks and privacy care.</li>
        <li>Judging AI output for a client who cannot judge it alone.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Tool familiarity alone is not proof of high income. The pay goes to people who connect AI to a client's real problem and show the result.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">Check before you commit</h2>

  <p>
    The four questions test whether a skill fits you, and the three proofs show you can deliver it, so use them together before you spend months on a skill.
  </p>

  <p class="check-label">Four questions to answer before you commit</p>

  <div class="protocol-stack">
    {checkpointItems.map((item) => (
      <div class="checkpoint">
